Notes
===============================================================================

Why this replaced a blanket "All Rights Reserved" (2026-09-20): the previous
text forbade forking, which is not a restriction this repository can impose.
Publishing a repository publicly on GitHub grants every GitHub user the right to
view and fork it under GitHub's Terms of Service (section D.5). A licence whose
headline term is void on the platform hosting it is worse than no licence for a
repository whose purpose is to be read as a work sample — the code is published
to be judged, so the code is now MIT. What actually needed protecting was never
the code: it was the personal and biographical content, and that is section 2.

For anything not covered here, or for use of section 2 or 3 material:
dashti.dat@gmail.com
